==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|akwisī|lang=gem-pro}}, possibly from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|h₂ek-||sharp, pointed|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|axa|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|akus|lang=osx}} (Low German {{term|Ax|Ax, Äx, Ex|lang=nds}}), Dutch {{term|aaks|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|ackus|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Axt|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|øx|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌵𐌹𐌶𐌹|tr=aqizi|lang=got|sc=Goth}}.

